---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const locale = 'en' as const;
---
<GuideLayout
  locale={locale}
  canonicalPath="/guides/space-requirements-small-bakery/"
  guideTitle="Space Requirements — Small Bakery Layout"
  title="Space Requirements for Bakery Tray Washer — Small Kitchen Layout"
  description="How much floor space does a JD-3 bakery tray washer need? Footprint, clearances, ventilation, drainage — practical layout tips for small bakery kitchens."
>
  <h1 class="mb-4">Space Requirements for a Bakery Tray Washer</h1>
  <p class="text-lg text-bakery-navy/80 mb-8">Small commercial kitchens are tight. Here's exactly how much space a JD-3 needs — and how to integrate it without losing prep area.</p>

  <h2 class="mb-3">Basic Footprint</h2>
  <p>The JD-3's machine dimensions are <strong>804 × 816 mm</strong> at the base. Plan for 850 × 850 mm of dedicated floor space (machine + minor positioning clearance).</p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">Required Clearances</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mt-3">
    <li><strong>Front clearance (operator side):</strong> 600 mm minimum. This is where the operator stands to load and unload racks.</li>
    <li><strong>Right side clearance:</strong> 100 mm minimum for ventilation. 400 mm recommended if this is your service-access side.</li>
    <li><strong>Left side clearance:</strong> 100 mm minimum.</li>
    <li><strong>Rear clearance:</strong> 150 mm minimum for plumbing and electrical connections.</li>
    <li><strong>Vertical clearance (above):</strong> 2,200 mm minimum so the hood can lift fully.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="mt-3"><strong>Total functional space including clearances: approximately 1,450 mm wide × 1,500 mm deep.</strong></p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">Loading Configuration Examples</h2>

  <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2">Layout 1: Adjacent to 3-bay sink</h3>
  <p>Position the JD-3 to the right of your existing 3-bay sink. Use the sink for pre-scrape and rinse, the JD-3 for wash. Total combined linear space: ~3.5 m. Works in most small commercial kitchens.</p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2">Layout 2: Dedicated dish corner</h3>
  <p>Position the JD-3 in a corner of the kitchen with a small staging counter to the side. Operator pivots between the staging counter and the JD-3. Linear space: ~2 m. Best for very small bakeries with limited floor area.</p>

  <h3 class="mt-6 mb-2">Layout 3: Pass-through dish pit</h3>
  <p>For bakeries with separate prep and service areas: install the JD-3 on a wall between the two, with loading on the dirty side and unloading on the clean side. Requires custom millwork. Best practice for hygiene-sensitive operations like patisserie.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">Floor Surface Requirements</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mt-3">
    <li>Level surface — JD-3 has adjustable feet for ±20 mm leveling</li>
    <li>Waterproof flooring (epoxy, sealed tile, stainless) — water will splash during loading/unloading</li>
    <li>Drain in the floor recommended (most commercial kitchens already have one)</li>
    <li>Non-slip surface — wet floors are common in dish areas</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">Ventilation</h2>
  <p>The JD-3's sealed hood reduces steam output by ~70% versus older machines, but some humidity escape is unavoidable. Recommendations:</p>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mt-3">
    <li>Position the JD-3 within reach of your existing kitchen exhaust hood (most common solution)</li>
    <li>For dedicated dish rooms: a small extraction fan (200 CFM) is sufficient</li>
    <li>Avoid positioning the JD-3 directly under a low ceiling without ventilation — humidity will accumulate</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">Plumbing</h2>
  <p>Required within 1.5 m of the JD-3 location:</p>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mt-3">
    <li>Cold water supply with G 3/4" connection point</li>
    <li>Floor drain or wall drain (G 1½" or larger)</li>
    <li>If the drain is above the machine: optional drain pump can push wastewater up to 2 m vertically</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">Power Outlet Location</h2>
  <p>The 380V three-phase outlet should be:</p>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mt-3">
    <li>Within 1.5 m of the JD-3 position</li>
    <li>Wall-mounted, not floor-mounted (water splashing)</li>
    <li>Above 600 mm height to stay clear of mop water</li>
    <li>Accessible without moving the machine (for emergency disconnect)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">If Your Kitchen Is Very Small</h2>
  <p>For kitchens under 30 m² where dedicating 1.5 × 1.5 m to a dishwasher feels impossible:</p>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mt-3">
    <li>Consider replacing your 3-bay sink with a 1-bay + JD-3 combo. You retain the prep sink function and add the dishwasher in roughly the same floor space.</li>
    <li>Consider a wall-mounted shelf above the JD-3 for racks. Vertical storage saves floor space.</li>
    <li>Schedule a virtual layout review with our team — we'll annotate your floor plan with placement options.</li>
  </ul>
</GuideLayout>
